(>> Solution to Question 5:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Demonstrate the mathematical formulation and NumPy implementation of 1D signal convolution and FIR filtering.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Discrete Linear Convolution:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Given an input discrete signal $x[n]$ of length $N$ and an impulse response filter $h[n]$ of) Tj
T*
(   length $M$, the output $y[n]$ is formulated as:) Tj
T*
(   $$y[n] = \(x * h\)[n] = \\sum_{k=-\\infty}^{\\infty} x[k] h[n - k]$$) Tj
T*
(   The total duration of the full linear convolution is $L = N + M - 1$.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   NumPy Implementation:) Tj
T*
(   ```python) Tj
T*
(   import numpy as np) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Define 1 kHz sampling rate, 100 ms test signal) Tj
T*
(   fs = 1000.0) Tj
T*
(   t = np.linspace\(0, 0.1, int\(0.1 * fs\), endpoint=False\)) Tj
T*
(   x = np.sin\(2 * np.pi * 50 * t\) + 0.5 * np.random.randn\(len\(t\)\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # 5-point moving average low-pass FIR filter) Tj
T*
(   h = np.ones\(5\) / 5.0) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Convolve using mode='same' to preserve original length) Tj
T*
(   y_clean = np.convolve\(x, h, mode='same'\)) Tj
T*
(   ```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Frequency Domain Acceleration:) Tj
T*
(   For large filters \($M > 64$\), direct time-domain convolution $O\(NM\)$ is replaced by FFT-based) Tj
T*
(   fast convolution via the Convolution Theorem: $y = \\text{IFFT}\(\\text{FFT}\(x\) \\cdot) Tj
T*
(   \\text{FFT}\(h\)\)$, running in $O\(\(N+M\) \\log\(N+M\)\)$ time.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 6:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the Discrete Fourier Transform \(DFT\) mathematical formulation and spectral analysis using `np.fft`.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Mathematical DFT Formulation:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   For a discrete-time signal $x[n]$ of length $N$ sampled at frequency $f_s$, the forward DFT is) Tj
T*
(   defined as:) Tj
T*
(   $$X[k] = \\sum_{n=0}^{N-1} x[n] \\cdot e^{-j \\frac{2\\pi}{N} k n}, \\quad k = 0, 1, \\dots, N-1$$) Tj
T*
(   Each bin $k$ corresponds to continuous physical frequency $f_k = \\frac{k \\cdot f_s}{N}$.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Spectral Analysis Workflow:) Tj
T*
(   ```python) Tj
T*
(   import numpy as np) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   fs = 8000.0 # 8 kHz audio sampling rate) Tj
T*
(   N = 1024) Tj
T*
(   t = np.arange\(N\) / fs) Tj
T*
(   sig = np.sin\(2 * np.pi * 440 * t\) + 0.5 * np.sin\(2 * np.pi * 1200 * t\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

endstream
