(   [Problem Statement]: Describe matrix decompositions in `np.linalg`: LU, QR, Cholesky, and Singular Value Decomposition \(SVD\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Key Matrix Decompositions in Engineering:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. QR Decomposition \(`np.linalg.qr`\):) Tj
T*
(   Decomposes $A \\in \\mathbb{R}^{m \\times n}$ into an orthogonal matrix $Q$ \($Q^T Q = I$\) and) Tj
T*
(   upper triangular matrix $R$: $A = QR$. Fundamental for linear least-squares problems and) Tj
T*
(   Gram-Schmidt orthogonalization.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Cholesky Decomposition \(`np.linalg.cholesky`\):) Tj
T*
(   For a symmetric positive-definite matrix $A$, factors $A = L L^T$ where $L$ is a lower) Tj
T*
(   triangular matrix with positive diagonal entries. Requires half the operations of LU) Tj
T*
(   decomposition; used in Kalman filtering and Gaussian processes.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Singular Value Decomposition \(SVD, `np.linalg.svd`\):) Tj
T*
(   Decomposes any matrix $A \\in \\mathbb{R}^{m \\times n}$ into:) Tj
T*
(   $$A = U \\Sigma V^H$$) Tj
T*
(   where $U$ and $V$ are unitary matrices and $\\Sigma$ contains non-negative singular values) Tj
T*
(   $\\sigma_1 \\ge \\sigma_2 \\ge \\dots \\ge 0$. Applications: Principal Component Analysis \(PCA\),) Tj
T*
(   pseudo-inverse calculation, MIMO channel rank determination.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
