(   [Problem Statement]: Explain eigenvalues and eigenvectors in circuit stability and state-space analysis using `np.linalg.eig`.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   State-Space Linear System Stability:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Continuous-time linear dynamical systems \(such as RLC resonant networks\) are represented in) Tj
T*
(   state-space form:) Tj
T*
(   $$\\dot{x}\(t\) = A x\(t\) + B u\(t\)$$) Tj
T*
(   System stability is governed by the eigenvalues $\\lambda_i$ of system matrix $A$, satisfying) Tj
T*
(   the characteristic equation $\\det\(A - \\lambda I\) = 0$.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Stability Criteria:) Tj
T*
(   1. Asymptotically Stable: $\\text{Re}\(\\lambda_i\) < 0$ for all eigenvalues \(all roots lie) Tj
T*
(   strictly in the open left-half complex plane LHP\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Marginally Stable: Purely imaginary eigenvalues $\\text{Re}\(\\lambda_i\) = 0$ with non-repeated) Tj
T*
(   algebraic multiplicity \(sinusoidal oscillator\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Unstable: Any eigenvalue with $\\text{Re}\(\\lambda_i\) > 0$ \(exponentially divergent response\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   NumPy Calculation:) Tj
T*
(   ```python) Tj
T*
(   import numpy as np) Tj
T*
(   A = np.array\([[-2.0, -5.0], [1.0, 0.0]]\)) Tj
T*
(   eigenvalues, eigenvectors = np.linalg.eig\(A\)) Tj
T*
(   is_stable = np.all\(np.real\(eigenvalues\) < 0\)) Tj
T*
(   ```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
