(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Memory-Mapped Arrays \(`np.memmap`\):) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   `np.memmap` allows reading and writing small segments of large binary datasets stored on disk) Tj
T*
(   directly into virtual memory via the OS kernel's `mmap\(\)` system call.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Mechanics and Advantages:) Tj
T*
(   - On-Demand Page Paging: Only requested 4 KB virtual memory pages are loaded from disk into RAM) Tj
T*
(   when accessed by slicing, preventing Out-Of-Memory \(OOM\) errors.) Tj
