T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Einstein Summation Convention:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   `np.einsum` provides a concise subscript syntax to specify complex tensor contractions,) Tj
T*
(   products, and transpositions without temporary intermediate array allocations:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Common Formulations:) Tj
T*
(   1. Matrix Multiplication: $C_{ik} = \\sum_j A_{ij} B_{jk}$) Tj
T*
(   `C = np.einsum\('ij,jk->ik', A, B\)`) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Matrix Trace: $\\text{Tr}\(A\) = \\sum_i A_{ii}$) Tj
T*
(   `tr = np.einsum\('ii->', A\)`) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Batch Matrix Multiplication: Given batch tensors $A \\in \\mathbb{R}^{B \\times M \\times K}$) Tj
T*
(   and $B \\in \\mathbb{R}^{B \\times K \\times N}$:) Tj
T*
(   `C = np.einsum\('bmk,bkn->bmn', A, B\)`) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   `np.einsum` evaluates optimal loop orders \(`optimize=True`\) to minimize memory bandwidth and) Tj
T*
(   temporary array overhead.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
