(   [Problem Statement]: Formulate numerical differentiation techniques in NumPy: Forward, Backward, and Central differences with error orders.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Numerical Differentiation Formulations:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Given discrete function evaluations $f\(x\)$ at uniform spacing $h$:) Tj
T*
(   1. Forward Difference:) Tj
T*
(   $$f'\(x\) \\approx \\frac{f\(x + h\) - f\(x\)}{h}, \\quad \\text{Truncation Error: } \\mathcal{O}\(h\)$$) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Backward Difference:) Tj
T*
(   $$f'\(x\) \\approx \\frac{f\(x\) - f\(x - h\)}{h}, \\quad \\text{Truncation Error: } \\mathcal{O}\(h\)$$) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Central Difference:) Tj
T*
(   $$f'\(x\) \\approx \\frac{f\(x + h\) - f\(x - h\)}{2h}, \\quad \\text{Truncation Error: }) Tj
T*
(   \\mathcal{O}\(h^2\)$$) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   NumPy's `np.gradient\(f, h\)` uses central differences for all interior points and second-order) Tj
T*
(   one-sided differences at boundaries, maintaining uniform $\\mathcal{O}\(h^2\)$ accuracy across the) Tj
T*
(   entire array.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

