(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the composite Trapezoidal and Simpson's rules for numerical integration using NumPy.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Numerical Quadrature Formulas:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. Composite Trapezoidal Rule \(`np.trapz`\):) Tj
T*
(   Approximates the area under $f\(x\)$ by summing trapezoids between uniform points $x_0, x_1,) Tj
T*
(   \\dots, x_N$ spaced by $h$:) Tj
T*
(   $$\\int_a^b f\(x\) dx \\approx \\frac{h}{2} \\left[ f\(x_0\) + 2 \\sum_{i=1}^{N-1} f\(x_i\) + f\(x_N\)) Tj
T*
(   \\right]$$) Tj
T*
(   Truncation Error: $\\mathcal{O}\(h^2\)$.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Composite Simpson's 1/3 Rule \(`scipy.integrate.simpson`\):) Tj
T*
(   Fits quadratic parabolas through successive triplets of points \(requires odd number of points) Tj
T*
(   $N+1$\):) Tj
T*
(   $$\\int_a^b f\(x\) dx \\approx \\frac{h}{3} \\left[ f\(x_0\) + 4 \\sum_{i=1,3,\\dots}^{N-1} f\(x_i\) + 2) Tj
T*
(   \\sum_{i=2,4,\\dots}^{N-2} f\(x_i\) + f\(x_N\) \\right]$$) Tj
T*
(   Truncation Error: $\\mathcal{O}\(h^4\)$, delivering substantially superior accuracy for smooth) Tj
T*
(   waveforms.) Tj
T*
() Tj
