(   Given $N$-point DFT $X[k] = \\sum_{n=0}^{N-1} x[n] W_N^{k n}$ where $W_N = e^{-j) Tj
T*
(   \\frac{2\\pi}{N}}$ and $N$ is a power of 2.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Split $x[n]$ into even-indexed samples $x[2m]$ and odd-indexed samples $x[2m+1]$ \($m = 0,) Tj
T*
(   \\dots, N/2 - 1$\):) Tj
T*
(   $$X[k] = \\sum_{m=0}^{N/2-1} x[2m] W_N^{k\(2m\)} + \\sum_{m=0}^{N/2-1} x[2m+1] W_N^{k\(2m+1\)}$$) Tj
T*
(   Noting that $W_N^{2 m k} = W_{N/2}^{m k}$:) Tj
T*
(   $$X[k] = E[k] + W_N^k O[k]$$) Tj
T*
(   $$X[k + N/2] = E[k] - W_N^k O[k]$$) Tj
T*
(   where $E[k]$ and $O[k]$ are $N/2$-point DFTs.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Computational Complexity Savings:) Tj
T*
(   - Direct DFT: $N^2$ complex multiplications.) Tj
T*
(   - Radix-2 FFT: $\\frac{N}{2} \\log_2 N$ complex multiplications.) Tj
T*
(   - For $N = 1024$:) Tj
T*
(   - Direct DFT: $1024^2 = 1,048,576$ multiplications.) Tj
T*
(   - FFT: $512 \\times 10 = 5,120$ multiplications.) Tj
T*
