(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Low-Rank Approximation via Eckart-Young-Mirsky Theorem:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Any noisy data matrix $A \\in \\mathbb{R}^{m \\times n}$ can be decomposed via SVD: $A =) Tj
T*
(   \\sum_{i=1}^r \\sigma_i u_i v_i^T$.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   ```python) Tj
T*
(   import numpy as np) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def denoise_tsvd\(A, k_components\):) Tj
T*
(   U, s, Vt = np.linalg.svd\(A, full_matrices=False\)) Tj
T*
(   # Keep only the top k dominant singular values) Tj
T*
(   s_filtered = np.zeros_like\(s\)) Tj
T*
(   s_filtered[:k_components] = s[:k_components]) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Reconstruct optimal rank-k low-noise matrix) Tj
T*
(   A_denoised = \(U * s_filtered\) @ Vt) Tj
T*
(   return A_denoised) Tj
T*
(   ```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   This filters out unstructured additive noise that populates the smaller tail singular values) Tj
T*
(   while preserving core correlated signal features.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
