(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the implementation and performance optimization of vectorized N-body gravitational or electromagnetic simulation.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   In Coulomb's law or gravitational simulation, computing pairwise forces between $N$ charged) Tj
T*
(   particles naively requires $O\(N^2\)$ nested loops.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   Vectorized Broadcasting Implementation:) Tj
T*
(   ```python) Tj
T*
(   import numpy as np) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def compute_pairwise_coulomb_forces\(pos, charges, k_e=8.9875e9\):) Tj
T*
(   # pos shape: \(N, 3\)) Tj
T*
(   # Broadcast difference vectors: \(N, 1, 3\) - \(1, N, 3\) -> \(N, N, 3\)) Tj
T*
(   r_vec = pos[:, np.newaxis, :] - pos[np.newaxis, :, :]) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Compute scalar distance cubed with epsilon softening) Tj
T*
(   dist_sq = np.sum\(r_vec**2, axis=-1\) + 1e-12) Tj
T*
(   dist_cube = dist_sq * np.sqrt\(dist_sq\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Charge products: \(N, 1\) * \(1, N\) -> \(N, N\)) Tj
T*
(   q_prod = charges[:, np.newaxis] * charges[np.newaxis, :]) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Force matrix: \(N, N, 3\)) Tj
T*
(   F_matrix = k_e * q_prod[:, :, np.newaxis] * r_vec / dist_cube[:, :, np.newaxis]) Tj
T*
(   # Total net force on each particle: sum over j) Tj
T*
(   return np.sum\(F_matrix, axis=1\)) Tj
T*
(   ```) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
