12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Detail NumPy memory management: PyArrayObject, buffer sharing, views, base attributes, and garbage collection.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   NumPy C-Architecture Memory Internals:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   1. `PyArrayObject` Struct:) Tj
T*
(   - `data`: Pointer to raw memory buffer \(`char *`\).) Tj
T*
(   - `nd`: Number of dimensions \(int\).) Tj
T*
(   - `dimensions`: Pointer to array of dimension sizes \(`npy_intp *`\).) Tj
T*
(   - `strides`: Pointer to array of byte steps \(`npy_intp *`\).) Tj
T*
(   - `base`: Pointer to parent `PyObject` that actually owns the memory buffer.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Buffer Sharing and `base` Attribute:) Tj
T*
(   - When `a` is created from scratch, `a.base is None` \(or owns memory\).) Tj
T*
(   - When `b = a[1:5]` is sliced, `b.base is a`. The base attribute holds a reference to `a`,) Tj
T*
(   incrementing its reference counter.) Tj
T*
(   - Garbage Collection Safety: Even if `del a` is executed, the raw memory buffer remains active) Tj
T*
(   and accessible in RAM as long as `b` exists because `b.base` holds a live reference to the) Tj
T*
(   underlying memory block.) Tj
T*
ET

