(>> Solution to Question 30:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Implement an adaptive Least Mean Squares \(LMS\) adaptive filter in NumPy for active noise cancellation.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Active Noise Cancellation via LMS Adaptive Filter:) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   ```python) Tj
T*
(   import numpy as np) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def lms_filter\(desired, reference, num_taps=32, mu=0.01\):) Tj
T*
(   N = len\(desired\)) Tj
T*
(   weights = np.zeros\(num_taps\)) Tj
T*
(   output = np.zeros\(N\)) Tj
T*
(   error = np.zeros\(N\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   for n in range\(num_taps, N\):) Tj
T*
(   # Extract reference sample window in reverse order) Tj
T*
(   x_window = reference[n:n - num_taps:-1]) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Estimate noise via FIR dot product) Tj
T*
(   y_noise_est = np.dot\(weights, x_window\)) Tj
T*
(   output[n] = y_noise_est) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Error signal \(clean desired output\)) Tj
T*
(   e = desired[n] - y_noise_est) Tj
T*
(   error[n] = e) Tj
T*
ET

